WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.167 --> 00:00:02.300
-Today's Friday,
and that's usually

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:03.601
when I catch up with
some personal stuff.

00:00:03.601 --> 00:00:04.834
I check my inbox,
return some e-mails,

00:00:04.834 --> 00:00:06.868
and, of course, I send out
thank-you notes.

00:00:06.868 --> 00:00:09.868
And I was just...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:09.868 --> 00:00:11.200
...running a bit behind.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.701
I thought, today,
if you guys wouldn't mind,

00:00:12.701 --> 00:00:16.434
I would just like to write out
my weekly thank-you notes.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.467
Is that cool?

00:00:17.467 --> 00:00:19.000
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:20.267
Thank you very much.

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:21.367
James, can I get some

00:00:21.367 --> 00:00:22.767
thank-you-note-writing music,
please?

00:00:22.767 --> 00:00:23.601
Thank you so much.

00:00:23.601 --> 00:00:26.100
[ Somber piano music playing ]

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.701
-[ Chuckles ]

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:30.501
-He forgot his tie again.

00:00:30.501 --> 00:00:32.033
[ Music stops ]
Mm.

00:00:35.534 --> 00:00:37.067
[ Music resumes ]

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.868
"Thank you,
Trump indictment protests,

00:00:39.868 --> 00:00:42.400
for looking like one guy decided
to dry his beach towels

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:44.334
in front of Trump Tower."
[ Music stops ]

00:00:44.334 --> 00:00:47.000
[ Laughter and applause ]
There are four there.

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:52.868
[ Music resumes ]

00:00:52.868 --> 00:00:56.200
"Thank you, TikTok stars
marching in Washington,

00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.701
for being the first time
a protest chant ends with,

00:00:58.701 --> 00:01:00.133
'Sheeeesh!'"

00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:02.133
[ Music stops ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:07.601
[ Music resumes ]

00:01:07.601 --> 00:01:10.868
"Thank you, spring, for being
when the flowers bloom,

00:01:10.868 --> 00:01:14.033
the birds sing, and the bears
come out of hibernation

00:01:14.033 --> 00:01:15.534
to look for cocaine."

00:01:15.534 --> 00:01:17.868
[ Music stops ]
[ Laughter ]

00:01:23.701 --> 00:01:25.234
[ Music resumes ]

00:01:25.234 --> 00:01:28.100
"Thank you, allergy medicine,
for being the reason

00:01:28.100 --> 00:01:30.367
I don't sneeze
through my kid's recital,

00:01:30.367 --> 00:01:32.167
but snore through it instead."

00:01:32.167 --> 00:01:34.501
[ Music stops ]
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:38.634 --> 00:01:40.033
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:40.033 --> 00:01:41.334
[ Music resumes ]

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:44.968
"Thank you, barbed wire, for not
going by your other name,

00:01:44.968 --> 00:01:46.334
Evil Slinky."

00:01:46.334 --> 00:01:49.200
[ Music stops ]
[ Laughs ]

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.734
[ Drum beat ]

00:01:51.734 --> 00:01:54.200
That's a jam.
Come on, man.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:57.267
That's a jam.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:01:58.767
[ Piano music resumes ]

00:01:58.767 --> 00:02:01.734
"Thank you, 'John Wick 4,'
'Shazam! 2,'

00:02:01.734 --> 00:02:03.868
'Scream VI,' and 'Creed III,'

00:02:03.868 --> 00:02:05.901
for sounding more like
a bingo card

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:07.634
than a weekend at the movies."

00:02:07.634 --> 00:02:10.367
Oh, I got it! Bingo!
[ Music stops ]

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:16.334
[ Music resumes ]

00:02:16.334 --> 00:02:20.100
"Thank you, birdhouses,
for being nature's Airbnbs."

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:22.300
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

